DISCOVERY DEMAND C — PROTECTIVE ORDER ENFORCEMENT RECORD

CASE: 1FDV-23-0001009
TO: Scot Stuart Brower, Esq. (Mother's Counsel)

DEFENDANT DEMANDS complete production of:

1. All documents regarding issuance of the Protective Order
2. All evidence supporting issuance (affidavits, testimony, exhibits)
3. All communications between court and parties regarding the order
4. All requests for modification or termination of the order
5. All violations or enforcement actions under the order
6. All communications between mother and her counsel regarding the order
7. Timeline of dates the order was served, filed, and recorded

IF THE PROTECTIVE ORDER WAS ISSUED WITHOUT PROPER HEARING: Mother must provide sworn certification that the order was issued with proper notice and opportunity to be heard per HRS Chapter 586.

RESPONSE DUE: 14 calendar days from service
FORMAT: Native electronic file format

STATUTORY BASIS: HRS Chapter 586 requires proper notice and hearing. Ex parte orders are void if no emergency existed.
